"Back Room - Smith's Quarters"
"This small back room has been built directly against the limestone blocks of
the castle wall.  Cold, green-tinged blocks of stone line the west and north
walls, while a sturdily constructed wall of wooden planks lies to the south. 
The area is evidently used as a sleeping chamber for the smith and his
apprentice; personal effects cover a shelf against the north wall and a pile
of discarded clothing lies next to one of the straw mattresses.  A heavy
leather curtain blocks off the heat and light from the forge to the east.
"
