"On the Stable Roof"
"This perch two dozen feet above the stone cobblestones of the courtyard offers
a grand vantage point to view the keep's layout.  Smoke rises slowly from the
northern end of the courtyard, where the dim ring of hammering can be heard
echoing off the stone walls.  Further north is a high wall; thicker smoke
rises from beyond the wall although its source is blocked from view.  A
towering stone tower dwarfs the eastern wall of the castle, its stone a
gleaming white against the dingy grey of the limestone walls.  The roof here
is made of wide, thin limestone slabs, some cracked with age.  The wall to the
south and west blocks any view of that section of the castle and is too smooth
to climb.  A few vines curl over the edge of the roof and have twined
searching roots between the cracked slabs of the roof.
"
